<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-24">24 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Nicolaus Copernicus dies in Frombork</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Copernicus died weeks after his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/de-revolutionibus-orbium-coelestium">On the Revolutions of the Heavenly Spheres</a> was printed; tradition says he saw a copy on his deathbed. His Sun-centred model began a revolution in astronomy.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-12">12 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Henry VIII marries Catherine Parr, his sixth wife</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a> married the twice-widowed Catherine Parr at Hampton Court. She outlived him, helped reconcile the king with his daughters and became the first English queen to publish a book in her own name.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-wayna-daga">Battle of Wayna Daga</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Wayna Daga was fought on 21 February 1543 in the Ethiopian highlands, where Emperor Galawdewos of the Ethiopian Empire, aided by Portuguese musketeers, defeated and killed Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Ghazi, known as Ahmad Gran.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-venlo">Treaty of Venlo</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Venlo was concluded on 7 September 1543 between Emperor Charles V and Duke William of Jülich-Cleves-Berg.</p></div></li></ol></section>
